The **long head of the biceps tendon (LHBT)** arises from the supraglenoid tubercle and superior glenoid labrum, passes through the glenohumeral joint, and exits via the bicipital groove. It lies **within the joint capsule** (intracapsular) but is **completely enveloped by its own synovial sheath** — a tubular reflection of the synovial membrane — which excludes it from the joint cavity proper (extrasynovial).
