This is a classic, high-yield presentation of osteoid osteoma — the triad of young male, night pain waking from sleep, and dramatic relief with aspirin/NSAIDs is essentially pathognomonic and should trigger immediate diagnosis before imaging.
Why NSAIDs specifically relieve the pain: The nidus of osteoid osteoma contains abundant prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) and unmyelinated nerve fibres. Aspirin and NSAIDs inhibit cyclo-oxygenase → reduce PGE2 production → dramatic pain relief. No other bone tumour shares this pharmacological response pattern.
