Lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) are classified according to the phase of micturition in which they occur: storage (filling), voiding (emptying), and post-micturition symptoms. Storage LUTS occur during the bladder filling phase and are classically remembered by the mnemonic FUN—Frequency, Urgency, Nocturia.
Therefore, frequency (1), nocturia (2), and urgency (5) are storage LUTS, whereas hesitancy (3) and straining (4) are voiding/obstructive LUTS, typically seen in bladder outlet obstruction such as BPH.
